    "version": "0.27.0",
    "body": "### New\n\n- **A Browser panel beside your threads, and a browser for the assistant.** Press `Ctrl+Shift+B` (`Cmd+Shift+B` on a Mac), use the globe in the thread header, or pick Browser in the command palette. It is a real web browser that Ancilla runs for you, with its own tabs and its own saved sign-ins, drawn in the panel: type an address or a search (anything that is not an address searches DuckDuckGo), go back, forward and reload, open links in new tabs, answer a page's dialogs, pick from its drop-down lists, upload files you choose from your computer, and copy and paste text. Typing works with accents and dead keys, so `ç`, `ã`, `~` then `a` and `´` then `e` come out right on a Brazilian keyboard, and *Open in my browser* hands a page to your own browser. It needs Edge, Chrome, Chromium or Brave on the computer.\n- **The assistant can look things up and work on the web, one approved site at a time.** Ask it, by voice or in text, to find something out and it opens the pages itself, in a private browser that forgets everything when it is done, and tells you what it found with the pages it came from. Each new site asks you first: the task waits under Assistant, Tasks as *Needs your OK*, and you answer *Allow for this task*, *Always allow*, *Not now* or *Block*; nothing is sent to a site before you do, whether it was typed in, linked or reached by a redirect. Per site, you can also opt in to sharing your saved sign-in from the Browser panel when an authenticated page is needed. Beyond reading pages, following links and filling inputs, the assistant can choose drop-down options, scroll, press keys, hover, wait, go back, and stage workspace files for upload (asking for your approval before attaching any file). The Browser panel shows it work live with a **Stop** button and **Sites it may open** so any site rule can be removed.\n- **The assistant asks each time before sending, posting, ordering or uploading on a page.** When a web task is about to send a form, attach a file, or click or press something named like buy, order, pay, send, post, delete or sign up (in English or Portuguese), it stops and shows you what it is about to do, on which page, and what will be sent: field names with their values, a password or card-like field hidden, a file by its name only. If the browser cannot tell which fields of a page are passwords, it hides every value and says so on the question instead of guessing. **Do it** does that one thing; **Don't**, or no answer in 10 minutes, does nothing and the page and the site stay as they were. It also never types into a password field or types a card number.\n- **Downloads behave like normal desktop downloads, with a native folder picker and remembered destination.** A file a page offers is fetched into a private staging folder first: a *Save this file?* dialog shows the name, size and site, the destination folder (the last one you used, else Downloads) with a native system folder picker (**Pick folder...** on Windows, macOS and Linux) or path entry, an optional **Remember this folder and save downloads automatically** preference, and **Save** or **Don't save**. Even with automatic saving enabled, programs and scripts (`.exe`, `.msi`, `.sh`, `.jar` and similar) still stop for your confirmation with a plain warning. Existing files are never overwritten (*name (1)*), files over 1 GB are cancelled, and unanswered or abandoned staging files are cleaned up automatically.\n- **Connect Gmail, Google Drive, Hostinger, GitHub, Supabase and Brevo.** Under Assistant, Connectors, Gmail and Google Drive sign in through official OAuth 2.0 with PKCE on a local loopback callback, refreshing expired tokens in the background and revoking tokens at Google when you press **Disconnect**; Hostinger, GitHub, Supabase and Brevo connect with an API token verified before it is saved. Every credential is stored in a file only your user account can read (`0600` on POSIX), credentials that appear in results are redacted, and every call is logged under Activity with **Switch**, **Test** and **Disconnect** one press away. Accounts start read-only with a curated list of read tools so untrusted content cannot talk a model into calling unlisted tools.\n- **Connector changes wait for your OK to the exact payload.** Under Assistant, Connectors, each write tier starts **Off**: reversible changes, changes other people see, and changes that cannot be undone. When enabled, any write proposal (creating branches, issues, comments or pull requests in GitHub; saving drafts or sending mail in Gmail; creating folders or text notes in Google Drive; updating DNS records or restarting a VPS in Hostinger) pauses the task as *Needs your OK* and shows the exact account, tool and arguments from the call itself. **Do it** approves that exact fingerprint once for ten minutes; changing a single character asks again, and untrusted input read earlier in the task triggers explicit warnings on the approval card.\n- **Tasks and model calls work across Muse, cloud APIs and local model servers.** Model access now supports Muse CLI, the common `/v1/chat/completions` protocol, the `/v1/messages` API, and auto-detected local servers (`Ollama`, `LM Studio`, `llama.cpp` and `vLLM`). When Muse CLI is not installed or unavailable, assistant read, write and check steps run directly on your configured model with workspace-confined tools (`read_file`, `list_dir`, `search_files`, `write_file`, `edit_file` and `run_check`), enforcing `realpath` confinement inside the project folder and requiring project writes to be enabled and approved.\n- **Voice calls gain optional HTTP speech servers, faster context, harness awareness and safer actions.** Alongside the built-in local ONNX speech engine, Assistant, Voice can use any `/audio/transcriptions` and `/audio/speech` server (hosted or local, with zero model download required). Partial speech pre-warms relevant memory notes while you are still talking so replies start sooner; short speaker echo is suppressed without re-feeding dismissed echo into the next turn; retried or interrupted turns deduplicate mutating proposals so actions are not proposed twice; five read-only harness tools let the call inspect running threads, messages, usage and projects; and spoken change requests create paused proposals on screen (*Needs your approval*) rather than changing files directly.\n- **Ancilla tells you when the assistant is waiting on you.** A change the voice proposed, a connector write, a web task asking before opening a site, submitting a page or saving a download, and a task that stopped to ask what to do raise one notification when you are not looking at the window, naming the task and why it waits without echoing untrusted page text.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **On Linux the Browser panel no longer goes silent.** Chromium on Linux can stop sending pictures of a tab when the tab is brought forward while its picture stream is running. The panel now activates the tab before starting its picture stream, restarts the stream or captures a fallback frame if a shown or resized tab stays quiet, and re-applies the viewport size after page load.\n- **A quiet page no longer leaves the Browser panel blank.** If no screencast frame arrives shortly after a tab is shown, the panel captures an initial frame directly.\n- **A local model server that cannot take native tool definitions no longer fails every call.** Servers or models that reject tool schemas now receive structured tool instructions through text fallback automatically, and **Test** reports whether tools work natively, through text, or not at all."
